WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:00.700
Hello there.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.480
I see you clicked on the video.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.120
I guess now you're wondering why.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.120
Good question.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.160
Well, first, obviously, the video had to exist for you to click on it.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.380
So, partly, you clicked on the video, because I made the video.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.080
But, of course, the video also needed to be shared on a public platform for you to see it and click on it

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.740
(which in this case was YouTube),

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.060
so I guess it's also because of YouTube that you clicked on the video.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.500
But YouTube only exists, because some guys named Chad Hurley, Jawed Karim and Steve Chen

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.020
made Youtube back in 2005.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.260
So, I guess it's because some guys named Chad, Jawed and Steve had met up in some point in their lives.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.060
But they were really only able to create YouTube, because of the Internet

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.660
and the Internet only exists, because of the guys who invented the Internet,

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.140
whose names are Robert E. Kahn and Vint Cerf.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.060
But they were only able to invent the Internet, because they had access to a programmable computer,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.800
which was invented by another guy named Konrad Zuse.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:53.880
Zuse invented the first programmable computer in 1938, which was built almost entirely out of thin metal sheets.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.880
So, technically, you clicked on this video, because metal exists.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.240
OK, so without YouTube, no video

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.480
without Internet, no YouTube

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.680
without computer, no Internet

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.320
without metal, no computer.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.560
But, where did metal come from?

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.100
Metal is primarily found in the Earth's crust, so metal comes from the Earth,

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.980
but the Earth only exists, because of a gas cloud that spun enough to condense and produce the Sun

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:17.100
and the Earth several billion years ago, which happened,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.240
because billions of years before that, the Big Bang occured to form time and space

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.400
and things to allow for things to happen

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.700
So, I guess you really only clicked on this video, because time and space and things

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.340
started 13.7 billion years ago.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.160
But, what about you?

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.460
You must have played a role in all this.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.660
I mean, you chose to be on YouTube, and you chose to click on this video.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:37.220
Right?

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.380
Well, why did you choose to be on YouTube right now,

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:44.480
as opposed to nearly an infinite amount of other things you could have chosen to do with your time?

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.420
And, what causes a video to appear on your YouTube feed, or wherever else you found it?

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.280
And why did you choose to click on it, instead of scrolling past it?

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.640
And, why are you someone with access to the Internet?

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.820
And, why do you even exist as a thing, that can know what the Internet is, in the first place?

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.280
The universe is made up of atoms, that function off of cause and effect patterns.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.960
13.7 billion years ago, the Big Bang ignited a string of events:

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.200
causes and effects, bumps and crashes, emergencies and emergence.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.300
Where everything became everything, in an exact order, in an exact amount of time.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.600
This sequence eventually led to the creation of a gas cloud, Earth,

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.440
metal, a guy named Konrad,

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.800
two more guys named Robert and Vint,

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.200
three more guys named Chad, Jawed and Steve,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.580
YouTube, this video,

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.380
and you, being here on YouTube, at this exact time, with your exact brain,

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.100
all in the perfect position for you to see this video and want to click on it.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.620
If this is true,

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.680
would that mean that all of this is predetermined?

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.000
Was I destined to create this video, you destined to see and click on it?

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.840
If right now, the universe stopped completely,

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.700
and everything dissolves back into nothing.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:45.060
You, me, this video

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.440
YouTube, the Internet, planet Earth

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.860
the Sun, the Galaxy, the universe.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.040
Everything just stopped.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.240
And then it all started over.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.200
The Big Bang occured all over again, just as it did 13.7 billion years ago.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:59.580
In 13.7 billion years from now, would you be here,

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.560
watching the same video all over again?

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:06.620
If the universe functions off of cause and effect sequences, carried out by the interaction of atoms,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:12.000
and you were made up of atoms, and your brain is made up of atoms, like everything else in this universe,

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.260
you exist in function, based off of cause and effect patterns.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:20.020
So, if the universe started over, exactly how it did 13.7 billion years ago,

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:23.340
just like how knocking down dominoes placed exactly the same way,

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.220
with the same wind and temperature conditions,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.640
would lead to the last domino falling in the exact same place, in the exact same amount of time,

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:30.700
every time.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:35.840
In 13.7 billion years from now, all the particles of the universe would have bumped and crashed and buzzed,

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.480
in the same order, creating the same Solar system,

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.080
Sun, Earth, metal, computer, Internet,

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.900
YouTube, this video, and you, watching it.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.760
So, after all that,

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.660
you clicked on this video, because you didn't have a choice.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:52.380
Now, you might argue that if I didn't title or thumbnail this video

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.760
in this way, you wouldn't have chosen to click on it,

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:58.020
and, therefore, you would have had freedom of choice, because of a reason.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.160
The reason being that you chose to click on it,

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.620
based on whether or not the tile or thumbnail provoked, or interested you.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:07.360
But why did this video's title, or thumbnail, provoke, or interest, you?

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:08.940
And, did you have any say in it?

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.820
In general, do you decide what interests you or not?

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:12.500
No.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.120
Things just do or don't.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.760
You are free to click on this video, because you wanted to,

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.280
but you weren't free to want to click on this video.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.280
To truly claim that you chose to click on this video on your own free will,

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.740
you would have had to have chosen whether or not you were exposed to this video,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.220
and if its title and thumbnail would interest you, prior to even knowing that the video existed.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.380
But you didn't do that, and you couldn't do that.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:37.100
You don't know why you decided to open up YouTube,

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.480
or whatever source brought you here.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.400
You don't know why you're interested in this video,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.940
you don't know why you clicked on it.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.060
You just did, because everything led you here.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.640
Arguably, it is impossible to argue that we have freewill.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:51.200
Our choices are determined by neurophysiological events in the brain,

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.920
which are determined by our genes, childhoods, and life experiences.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.040
All of which have wired our brains in a certain way.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.000
None of which we had any say in.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.240
Our lifes are determined by the forces of cause and effect, that exist outside of our control.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.560
The things that happened, that caused you to be born, you did not choose.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:11.880
The things that caused you to be born to your specific parents, in a certain part of the world, you did not choose.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.740
The things that caused you to be male or female, tall or small,

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.420
light or dark-skinned, you did not choose.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.120
The things that have passed by you, the words you have heard,

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.480
the feeling you've experienced,

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.840
you did not choose any of it, and you cannot choose what any of it will cause you to do

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:25.600
and feel.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.560
In this moment, or any other moment.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:31.280
Essentally, that means, that nothing you do is really your choice.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.240
And wouldn't that mean that there's no point in doing anything?

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.140
No point in trying?

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.580
No point in caring?

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.520
If we're no different than the atoms around and inside, of us,

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:43.620
operating with no control over their movements and placements in time and space,

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:46.740
then isn't everything we do meaningless, and not worth putting effort towards?

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:47.620
No,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.880
fortunately, for us, that is not the case.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.120
You can't truly choose who you are, or who you become,

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.440
you can't choose what happens, or has happened to you.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.320
But you can choose what to do with it all:

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.860
how to observe it, how to experience and embrace the movement of it.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.040
When you get in a car, you put a seatbelt on.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.260
Or, at least, you should.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:08.280
Even though you have no control over the conditions of the roads, and the other drivers on the roads,

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.720
you still put a seatbelt on.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.480
You have no choice in the fact that you know what a seatbelt is,

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:16.360
as well as no choice in the feeling of fear for what not having a seatbelt might cause.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:20.700
But your response to this knowledge and fear can still save your life if you are hit.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:24.760
You observed the knowledge and feeling towards putting a seatbelt on, so you do.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.980
And, if you are hit, this action can save you.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:31.560
Regardless of subjective choice, you are not an inactive participant in your life.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.220
Your participation, and actions, are necessary.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.640
You must try,

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.140
and care.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:40.760
Likewise, when you have a goal, dream, interest, passion, or curiosity,

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:45.060
you don't not do anything, because the universe predestined you to end up somewhere.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:48.980
Instead, you follow your goals, dreams, interests, passions, and curiosities.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:50.820
You respond to the world around them.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:51.980
You do things,

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.320
you find out where you'll end up.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:57.240
You click on the video, and you'll, hopefully, enjoy it.

